 rod shaped cells  and we're watching the enzymatic motions  of these processes as the cells are  re-emerging  so basically what the cell is machine  lets us do is very  rapidly turn on and off conditions or  insults  to individual things while following  singles  besides y4c y4d and b4a plate  we have launched another unique plate  for the east customers last year  y04t so besides the elastic ceiling  we add three elastic wall features  to for a trap to hold e cells for up to  12 hours and more let's look at the  trapping mechanism pictures on the right  when the cells are loaded with high flow  of media the cells will get randomly  trapped in one of the traps  this is specifically useful if you're  studying aging  and folk just want to focus on the  mother cells  or if you just want to study how long  they can keep generating daughter cells  it also becomes very useful if you want  to study mother daughter interactions  let's see the real trapping and culture  in action  in the video on the left it shows how  loading is done  you see individual heat cells gathering  around the chambers  and get randomly trapped in individual  traps  and in the photo shown on the right of  the slide you see the results of a  colony grown  from one single mother cell in our clay  after 24 hours of culture  and the special feature is that we  design the chambers in a way  that the flow can easily wash away the  excess cells so now the culture can go  up to 72 hours without clogging the  nutrient  or the treatment flow  and here's our newest plate  b04f launched early this year  that is specifically designed for  biofilm studies  there are two 200 micron by 200 micron  paths in one unit  because of the elastic pad design the  inner ring of the biofilms will always  be  in molar layer and in one focal plane so  that no matter how many millions of  cells are around  you can still clearly see the proteins  of interest get turned on  or off by turbidation perturbation  inside the bowel zone and because there  are only two paths with  significant spacing in between you can  study the communications  between the two biosomes that are some  distance apart  and we're confident to say that c zero  for f  is the one and only biofilm plate that  allow you  to image two biofilms at the same time  and it's the only lifestyle imaging  system that enables you to monitor the  communications between the two biofilms  here's the clap to show facilities  growing into a biofilm on our plate  as i mentioned in the previous slide the  inner ring of the biofilms are held in  one focal plane throughout the entire  culture  and we also observe the size of the  biofilm changes over time  which is also known as the periodic  growth of the biofilm  the size changes of the biofilm or the  so-called periodic  growth was identified by several  scientists  one of them was professor seoul at ucsd  he was able to use our previous  prototype to trap  and grow biofilms and introduce  environmental perturbation  and observe that biosome could grow and  reorganize and grow  again and reorganize again if you may  take this gene to remove the protein  the size wouldn't change he published a  paper on nature  and linked this protein with biofilm  periodic growth  he also published another nature paper  using our system to study the membrane  potential changes in the biofilms upon  perturbation  during the making of this biofilm plate  dr seoul and his team  have helped us identify the must-have  features  they also helped validate the function  of this plate  and now this play is commercially  available  there are many applications you can do  on our plate  like protein translocation protein  trafficking you can  track certain protein smoothies in the  cell  in the cell walls we can heat shock the  cells or introduce drugs  stress or gas change and see genes  turning on and off  you can study mitosis and how cells  divide  and we have many many customers that  have published on  nature